<!--BlockML Documentation — copy the A02 DocSet into A03
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task.A03_CopyDocSet-->
<task:A03_CopyDocSet xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that copies the A02 DocSet into A03
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A03 authoring task: create or update BmlDocSet_A03 by copying identity
    from BmlDocSet_A02 and remapping page / PageGroup slots onto A03 Blocks
    of the same name.

    - **Identity** — title, version, summary, and documentation come from
      BmlDocSet_A02
    - **Correspondence** — an A03 Page or PageGroup matches an A02 entry
      when the Block name is the same and only the sector package differs
    - **Slots** — pages, pageGroups, homePage, and rootPageGroup may list
      only A03 Blocks; A02 references are never kept
    - **Pages / groups** — this task does not create, edit, or empty A03
      Page or PageGroup files
    - **Sources** — this task has no authoritativeSources
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          All information for this task comes from BmlDocSet_A02 and from the
          A03 Pages and PageGroups that already exist. Do not read
          authoritativeSources on this task. Do not read BmlDocSetPlan as the
          identity source. Do not invent title, version, summary, or
          documentation that BmlDocSet_A02 does not state. Do not create or
          edit Pages, PageGroups, or pageMapping. Do not edit BmlDocSet_A02
          or any Block outside a03.

          1. Read the A02 DocSet
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.BmlDocSet_A02.
          Collect title, version, summary, documentation, is, and isNot.
          Those identity fields are what this task copies. Also collect the
          A02 pages and pageGroups compositions and the homePage and
          rootPageGroup values — those slots are remapped, never copied as
          A02 FQNs.

          2. Create A03 subpackages if they do not exist
          Under org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring, create these packages
          when they are missing:
          - data → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data
          - page → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page
          - pagegroup → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup

          Create only the package directories (the filesystem homes for the
          DocSet and for A03 pages and PageGroups). If a package already
          exists, leave it as is. Do not invent pages or PageGroups. Do not
          create packages outside a03.

          3. Resolve the A03 DocSet FQN
          DocSet FQN =
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.BmlDocSet_A03
          Write only this a03 DocSet, never a DocSet outside a03 (a02 or any
          later sector). Do not edit DocSets of other sectors.

          4. Map A02 page and PageGroup FQNs to A03 counterparts
          An A03 counterpart is the same Page or PageGroup in the A03
          package tree: the Block name is identical, and only the sector
          package changes (a02_structuring → a03_authoring). The remainder
          of the FQN after .data. is unchanged.

          Page FQN =
          replace the prefix org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page
          with org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page
          (for example
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.TableOfContents
          → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page.docs.TableOfContents).

          PageGroup FQN =
          replace the prefix
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup
          with org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup
          (for example
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.pagegroup.RootPageGroup
          → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup.RootPageGroup).

          A counterpart exists only when that A03 Block is already in the
          corpus. Confirm with inspect or scan; do not guess from the FQN
          alone. If no A03 Block with that name exists, omit the entry.
          Never fall back to the A02 FQN. Never invent a Page or PageGroup
          to complete a mapping.

          5. Create or update BmlDocSet_A03
          If BmlDocSet_A03 already exists, keep only the FQN / file path so
          the same Block is overwritten. Refresh title, version, summary,
          documentation, is, and isNot from BmlDocSet_A02. Rebuild pages,
          pageGroups, homePage, and rootPageGroup from the remapped A02
          slots (step 4). Do not edit any A03 Page or PageGroup file —
          existing A03 page and group configuration stays as it is.

          If BmlDocSet_A03 does not exist, create it as the A03 DocSet
          container. Example of the target shape:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data/BmlDocSet_A03.bml

          Each DocSet must:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.core.DocSet
          - use BmlDocSet_A03 as the Block name
          - set is from BmlDocSet_A02.is
          - set isNot from BmlDocSet_A02.isNot
          - set documentation from BmlDocSet_A02.documentation, replacing
            any A02-task sentences with: pages / homePage and pageGroups /
            rootPageGroup list only A03 counterparts of the A02 slots
          - override title from BmlDocSet_A02.title
          - override version from BmlDocSet_A02.version
          - override summary from BmlDocSet_A02.summary
          - declare aggregations pages and pageGroups
          - omit learningPaths
          - omit every other aggregation
          - never list an A02 Page or PageGroup in any slot

          Two situations:

          A. A03 has no Pages and no PageGroups yet
          Copy identity only. Leave pages and pageGroups as empty
          compositions. Omit homePage and rootPageGroup. The A03 DocSet
          is then an empty container: title, summary, version, is, isNot,
          and documentation are transferred; no Page or PageGroup slots
          are filled. Do not create Pages or PageGroups to populate them.

          B. A03 already has Pages and / or PageGroups
          Walk BmlDocSet_A02.pages in A02 order. For each A02 page, if an
          A03 counterpart exists, append that A03 Page to
          BmlDocSet_A03.pages; otherwise skip it. Walk
          BmlDocSet_A02.pageGroups the same way into
          BmlDocSet_A03.pageGroups. Resolve homePage and rootPageGroup
          the same way: use the A03 counterpart when it exists; omit the
          property when it does not. homePage, when set, must be one of
          the A03 pages in pages. rootPageGroup, when set, must be one of
          the A03 groups in pageGroups.

          BmlDocSet_A03.pages, pageGroups, homePage, and rootPageGroup
          may contain only a03 Pages and PageGroups. If an existing slot
          entry is outside a03, remove it. Do not keep an A02 reference
          because the A03 counterpart is missing. Do not add an A03 Page
          or PageGroup that has no A02 counterpart in the remapped lists.

          6. Export BmlDocSet_A03 from the catalog
          Export org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.BmlDocSet_A03
          from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not already in the
          catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of other sectors.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
</task:A03_CopyDocSet>
